@flexiarg operator/get-the-missing-account-by-narrated-stepping
@title Get The Missing Account By Narrated Stepping
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-ekuwTV turn-stEppf
@parent cycle-machine/step-machine
@context The records of what a system's parts do are missing or partial, and the system can be run step by step.

! conclusion: Run the machine stepped and narrated, then read the narration where it is written.

  + IF:
    The operator has an agent run it in a stepper and narrate each step in detail, and tells the other agent where to read.

  + HOWEVER:
    A narrated run covers one run only, and the narrator may invent activity for steps that do not act.

  + THEN:
    Run the machine stepped and narrated, then read the narration where it is written.

  + BECAUSE:
    Narration produces the account that the records lack.
